Following the release and success of her album ''[[Loud (Rihanna album)|Loud]]'' (2010), Rihanna originally revealed via [[Twitter]] that the album would be re-issued with new songs and released in Fall 2011, writing that "[t]he [''Loud'' era] continues with more new music to add to [your] collection".<ref name="BET">{{cite web|url=https://www.bet.com/article/6dwxi4/rihanna-to-re-release-loud|title=Rihanna to Re-Release Loud|publisher=[[Black Entertainment Television]]|date=2011-06-17|access-date=2011-09-19|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160410110929/http://www.bet.com/news/music/2011/06/17/rihanna-to-re-release-loud-.html|archive-date=2016-04-10|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="Fall2011">{{cite news|url=http://www.rap-up.com/2011/06/17/rihanna-to-release-new-album-this-fall/|title=Rihanna plans 'Loud' re-release for Fall|work=Rap-Up|date=2011-06-17|access-date=2011-09-19|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190328120049/https://www.rap-up.com/2011/06/17/rihanna-to-release-new-album-this-fall/|archive-date=2019-03-28|url-status=dead}}</ref> In September 2011, Rihanna again took to the [[social networking]] site to confirm that the plans had been scrapped, with the singer tweeting "I [thought about] a [re-release], but LOUD is its own body of work! Plus [you] guys work so hard that [you] deserve to act brand new".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://hellobeautiful.com/gossip-news/hellobeautifulstaff2/rihanna-loud-rerelease-scrapped/|title=Rihanna Scraps "Loud" Re-Release For New Album|work=Hello Beautiful!|publisher=[[BlackPlanet]]|date=2011-09-06|access-date=2011-09-19|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111001044123/http://hellobeautiful.com/gossip-news/hellobeautifulstaff2/rihanna-loud-rerelease-scrapped/|archive-date=2011-10-01|url-status=live}}</ref> On September 19, 2011, Rihanna further provoked excitement amongst her followers when she posted that she was listening to the song, only to be re-tweeted by [[Calvin Harris]], who replied "Sometimes it feels like we find love in the most hopeless place", suggesting that his response contained possible lyrics from the song.<ref name="USRadioPremiere"/> In an interview with [[The Capital FM Network|Capital FM]], Harris – who produced the track<ref name="SongProducer">{{cite news|url=http://www.rap-up.com/2011/09/19/rihanna-finds-love-on-new-single/|title=New Report: Rihanna finds 'Love' on new single|work=Rap-Up|date=2011-09-19|access-date=2011-09-19|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180210002324/http://www.rap-up.com/2011/09/19/rihanna-finds-love-on-new-single/|archive-date=2018-02-10|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.nme.com/news/rihanna/59294|title=Rihanna collaborates with Calvin Harris on new single|work=[[NME]]|date=2011-09-19|access-date=2011-09-19|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110924064328/http://www.nme.com/news/rihanna/59294|archive-date=2011-09-24|url-status=live}}</ref> – explained that followers of Rihanna had sent messages to him regarding their expectations of the song, saying "The song better not be rubbish", which he interpreted as slightly threatening, but went on to say that "it's all part of the fun".<ref>{{cite news|last=McCabe|first=Joanne|url=http://www.metro.co.uk/music/876433-calvin-harris-rihanna-navy-warned-me-we-found-love-better-be-good|title=Calvin Harris: Rihanna 'navy' warned me We Found Love better be quality|work=[[Metro (British newspaper)|Metro]]|date=2011-09-23|access-date=2011-09-23|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110925194912/http://www.metro.co.uk/music/876433-calvin-harris-rihanna-navy-warned-me-we-found-love-better-be-good|archive-date=2011-09-25|url-status=live}}</ref> In an interview for Q magazine, Harris said of the lyric, "we found love in a hopeless place," "It could have been Jumpin Jaks in [[Dumfries]] (Harris' home town), I don't know exactly what I was thinking about."{{citation needed|date=April 2014}}

"We Found Love" premiered in the United Kingdom on September 22, 2011, on Capital FM,<ref name="UKRadioPremiere">{{cite web|url=http://www.capitalfm.com/artists/rihanna/news/calvin-harris-we-found-love/|title=Rihanna Reveals New Single Title And Lyrics|publisher=[[The Capital FM Network]]|date=2011-09-22|access-date=2011-09-22|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170330055248/http://www.capitalfm.com/artists/rihanna/news/calvin-harris-we-found-love/|archive-date=2017-03-30|url-status=live}}</ref> and was sent for mainstream adds in the United States on October 11, 2011.<ref name="USRadioPremiere">{{cite web|last=Renshaw|first=David|url=http://popdash.com/news/6898/rihanna-label-confirms-we-found-love-to-premiere-friday|title=Rihanna Label Confirms 'We Found Love' To Premiere Friday|publisher=Popdash|date=2011-09-20|access-date=2011-09-20|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120113041312/http://popdash.com/news/6898/rihanna-label-confirms-we-found-love-to-premiere-friday|archive-date=2012-01-13|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="MTVRadioConfimation">{{cite web|last=Vena|first=Jocelyn|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1671029/rihanna-we-found-love-single.jhtml|title=Rihanna Confirms Next Single 'We Found Love'|publisher=MTV. Viacom|date=2011-09-20|access-date=2011-09-20|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121108015119/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1671029/rihanna-we-found-love-single.jhtml|archive-date=2012-11-08|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="MAINSTREAM"/> The song was released via [[iTunes]] on September 22, 2011.<ref name="iTunes">"We Found Love" digital single on various international iTunes stores on September 22, 2011:
